# ─── Superseded by a notebook ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only this one. The other .py files (canonicalize_words, decompose_letters,
# sofi_dynamic, sofi_streaming, pseudo_label, letter_features) are importable
# modules the notebooks depend on and are deliberately TRACKED -- do not add a
# blanket *.py rule here or the notebooks stop running on a fresh clone.
sofi_segmentation.py

# ─── Deliberately tracked, listed here so nobody "cleans them up" ───────────
# pseudo_labels.csv, pseudo_label_clips.csv, pseudo_label_segments.csv
# word_letter_mapping.json
# letter_sheets/*.png, spot_check/*.png
#
# These are regenerable ONLY by someone who has the 95MB keypoint CSV and the
# video corpus, neither of which is in git. For anyone else they are the
# primary evidence -- letter_sheets/ in particular is what shows the
# pseudo-labels are sound. Keeping them is the point, not an oversight.
#
# Caveat: PNGs do not delta-compress, so each regeneration adds its full size
# to history permanently. If the repo gets heavy, prune these from history
# rather than quietly deleting them from the working tree.

